   "line": [
    "Bg7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The key operation: meet the dark-bishop sortie with Bxh6, deflecting the queen away from the pawn on d4. It looks like it wrecks our castling, but the point is the centre — once we hit d4 with c5, the whole structure starts to buckle.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Trade to deflect the piece guarding a weak pawn, then strike that pawn with a break.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 1988.5,
   "fen": "rnbqk2r/ppp1ppbp/5npB/3p4/3P4/2N5/PPPQPPPP/R3KBNR b KQkq - 3 5",
   "line": [
    "Bh6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The broader lesson: don't reflexively answer Bh6 by castling short. Taking pulls your opponent's attention off the centre — Bh6 was premature, and after the trade we hit c5 and White can't hold the middle.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Answer a flank provocation by trading and counterpunching the centre, not by castling into it.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
